      "note": "Why the correction is needed."
    },
    "how_it_fires": "The corrector matches on the token's WARLI value, not on the source text. So a pair only fires when that spelling actually reaches the output — either because a dictionary entry carries a non-canonical form, or because a Hindi/Marathi token had no dictionary match and passed through unchanged. The second case makes this table a useful fallback layer for source words the dictionary does not yet cover."
